         "array": "u8",
         "count": 1
        },
        "optional": true
       },
       {
        "name": "fallout_behavior_flags",
        "type": {
         "flags": "u16",
         "bits": {
          "0": "Hellos To Player",
          "1": "Random Conversations",
          "2": "Observe Combat Behavior",
          "3": "Unknown 4",
          "4": "Reaction To Player Actions",
          "5": "Friendly Fire Comments",
          "6": "Aggro Radius Behavior",
          "7": "Allow Idle Chatter",
          "8": "Avoid Radiation"
         }
        },
        "optional": true
       },
       {
        "name": "type_specific_flags_raw",
        "type": "u16",
        "optional": true
       },
       {
        "name": "unused2",
        "type": {
         "array": "u8",
         "count": 2
        },
        "optional": true
       }
      ]
     },
     "confidence": "documented",
     "note": "xEdit wbDefinitionsFNV.pas PACK PKDT, SetOptionalFrom(2); flag names from wbDefinitionsCommon.pas wbPackageFlags (the FO3 names apply to FNV, wbIsFallout3 covers both games). Bit 20 is 'Head-Tracking Off' there and in the GECK wiki's flag list, 'Armor Unequipped' in JIP's GetPackageFlag list. The type-specific flags are a union decided by the package type (wbPKDTSpecificFlagsDecider): Find/Escort/Eat bits 8-10 Allow Buying/Killing/Stealing; Wander/Sandbox bits 0-5 No Eating/Sleeping/Conversation/Idle Markers/Furniture/Wandering; Use Item At bit 2 Sit Down plus 8-10; Ambush bit 0 Hide While Ambushing; Guard bit 3 Remain Near Reference to Guard. Kept as u16 here; fnv-ai reads it by type."
    },
    "PLDT": {
     "name": "Location 1",
     "type": "PackageLocation",
     "confidence": "documented",
     "note": "xEdit PACK PLDT; the location field is a union decided by the type (wbPxDTLocationDecider): 0 reference FormID, 1 cell FormID, 4 base object FormID, 5 object type (wbObjectTypeEnum), otherwise unused. Kept as u32; fnv-ai maps FormIDs by type."
    },
    "PLD2": {
     "name": "Location 2",
     "type": "PackageLocation",
     "confidence": "documented",
     "note": "xEdit PACK PLD2 (it appears twice in xEdit's list, the second as 'Location 2 (again??)'), same layout as PLDT"
    },
